      "writtenOn": "2020-11-12T18:53:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\"Intermittent\" meaning what - platform incorrectly dropping them, or due to a switch triggered by the carrier? The former is a bug, the latter is going to happen whether we like it or not. Carrier apps are smart enough to deal with this already and know when they lose/regain carrier privileges during a switch, so that\u0027s not a big deal.\n\nUsing SM#canManageSubscription is going to create an inequality between pSIM and eSIM profiles, where suddenly a VCN set up on the eSIM can be managed even when the profiles aren\u0027t active, whereas a VCN on a removed pSIM can\u0027t. Not worth the distinction IMO.",
      "parentUuid": "10fc1ab3_3f0d4db3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 178,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 178,
        "endChar": 43
